    {
      "source_block": 101,
      "source_title": "Supplementary Table S29. Donor-level single-cell effects with bootstrap confidence intervals. The complete table shipped in the deposit (06_single_cell/single_cell_donor_level_effects_with_ci.csv) has 208 rows: every audited comparison with at least three donors per arm carries a donor-level summary and a bootstrap 95% interval. The 240 audited comparisons reconcile as follows: 160 satisfy the test rules (72 paired, 56 donor-disjoint unpaired, 32 cell-identity) and additionally carry exploratory p and FDR columns; 48 carry a summary and interval but no test; and 32 carry no estimate because of insufficient donor representation. The 80 comparisons reported as not testable are the 48 with a summary plus the 32 without. All p and FDR values are exploratory.",
